 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A clothing label gives information about a garment:\n• the size (S, M, L, XL, or numbers such as 38, 40);\n• the fibre content (for example 65% polyester, 35% cotton);\n• the trade mark (brand) and country of manufacture;\n• the care instructions, often as symbols.\nCare symbols:\n• a tub with water: washing (a number shows the maximum temperature, a hand means hand wash only, a cross means do not wash);\n• a triangle: bleaching (crossed = do not bleach);\n• a square: drying (a circle inside = tumble dry);\n• an iron: ironing (dots show the heat: one dot cool, two warm, three hot; crossed = do not iron);\n• a circle: dry cleaning.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "A label shows an iron with one dot. How should the garment be ironed?",
  "steps": [
   "The dots on the iron show the heat.",
   "One dot means a cool iron (for synthetics such as nylon)."
  ],
  "answer": "With a cool iron.",
  "checks": []
 },
